{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/573981-dogs-of-war-revolutionary-war-setting-for-wolf","id":573981,"title":"Dogs of War: Revolutionary War setting for Wolf","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-30T08:32:27-07:00","id":573981,"title":"Dogs of War: Revolutionary War setting for Wolf","content":"Hello all. I'm kicking off my wolf game today, the setting is going to be in Boston Massachusetts 1776, at the beginning of the revolutionary war. <br /> <br /> There will be lots of war spirits, obviously conflict with human armed forces, and I have some plans for hunters and the hosts, but what do you guys think I should do with the pure?<br /> <br /> What are some of the things you think can be good about this setting, or ideas you'd add to the setting? <br /> <br /> I'll post updates on our sessions as I go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1898-wadesauce","name":"wadesauce","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1898_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T12:32:50-07:00","id":574198,"title":"","content":"Ivory claws are tied in with the British nobles and merchants. My suggestion is to take David Ick's theories and replace lizard with wolf, but tone it down a little bit compared to Ick's work.<br /> <br /> The involvement of the french and their royal family/nobles could suggest a clan war going on among the claws.<br /> <br /> Forsaken are going through a civil war too. Native American forsaken and those that are British loyalists are against the revolutionaries.<br /> <br /> Spirit courts of America are in chaos as conflicting ideals battle in the hisil.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T05:46:52-07:00","id":575088,"title":"","content":"Perhaps bring along a pack of Hessian Uratha, who followed the mercenaries fighting for the brits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T14:06:29-07:00","id":575601,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">[QUOTE=wadesauce;n573981]Hello all. I'm kicking off my wolf game today, the setting is going to be in Boston Massachusetts 1776, at the beginning of the revolutionary war.[</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">/QUOTE]</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The war broke out in April of 1775.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/573981-dogs-of-war-revolutionary-war-setting-for-wolf?p=574198#post574198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ivory claws are tied in with the British nobles and merchants. My suggestion is to take David Ick's theories and replace lizard with wolf, but tone it down a little bit compared to Ick's work.<br /> <br /> The involvement of the french and their royal family/nobles could suggest a clan war going on among the claws.</div> </div> </div> </div>Claws aren't just European nobility though. While not at the heights it'll reach in the 19th Century, racial supremacist ideology as tied to dominance over the enslaved, and the divine right of the white man to conquer Westward implies there'd be fair representation of the Ivory Claws among American Revolutionaries too, not just the European nobles on either side.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spirit courts of America are in chaos as conflicting ideals battle in the hisil.<br /> </div> </div> </div>Not that much chaos. I mean, the philosophical spirits are rising up to be more directly involved than in past conflicts, but it's not like the scale of the war itself was super-devastating compared to the other conflicts the continent had seen in recent history. I think from the perspective of the Hisil, war and plague are just the human version of a forest fire - it's just something that happens from time to time to clean out excess to allow new growth, as part of a natural cycle. World War I in particular will shake this concept by its unprecedented scale and industrialized power though.<br /> <br /> <br /> In terms of North America, if you're looking for &quot;a war that creates conflict in the Hisil over conflict ideals over what it means to be [insert national identity] and the meaning of [philosophical concept]; and was particularly chaotic due to its largely unprecedented scale&quot; - I'd look less at the 1770s and more at the 1860s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-01-2015, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T18:05:16-07:00","id":575842,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=glamourweaver;n575601]<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wadesauce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/573981-dogs-of-war-revolutionary-war-setting-for-wolf#post573981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello all. I'm kicking off my wolf game today, the setting is going to be in Boston Massachusetts 1776, at the beginning of the revolutionary war.[</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wadesauce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/573981-dogs-of-war-revolutionary-war-setting-for-wolf#post573981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">/QUOTE]</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The war broke out in April of 1775.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Claws aren't just European nobility though. While not at the heights it'll reach in the 19th Century, racial supremacist ideology as tied to dominance over the enslaved, and the divine right of the white man to conquer Westward implies there'd be fair representation of the Ivory Claws among American Revolutionaries too, not just the European nobles on either side.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not that much chaos. I mean, the philosophical spirits are rising up to be more directly involved than in past conflicts, but it's not like the scale of the war itself was super-devastating compared to the other conflicts the continent had seen in recent history. I think from the perspective of the Hisil, war and plague are just the human version of a forest fire - it's just something that happens from time to time to clean out excess to allow new growth, as part of a natural cycle. World War I in particular will shake this concept by its unprecedented scale and industrialized power though.<br /> <br /> <br /> In terms of North America, if you're looking for &quot;a war that creates conflict in the Hisil over conflict ideals over what it means to be [insert national identity] and the meaning of [philosophical concept]; and was particularly chaotic due to its largely unprecedented scale&quot; - I'd look less at the 1770s and more at the 1860s.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Maybe the more racist VS more nobility claws is a conflict that can be explored. I tend to use Ivory claw civil wars, over one thing or another, in my settings where that Tribe plays a large role.<br /> <br /> Claws are probably involved with the smugglers that had money to gain from rebellion, assuming iron masters and Storm lords haven't taken over that niche.<br /> <br /> I imagine that the fire touched would be on the side of the British simply because the secular humanist viewpoint of the founders, or at least the most famous of them, isn't compatible with their brand of religion.<br /> <br /> I don't know how the predator kings would react to the revolution.<br /> <br /> Ben Franklin has got to have some paranormal knowledge and Washington's stupid levels of good luck could have some interesting explanation. Culper Ring may include supernaturals, especially agent 355, since we still don't know who she was, which makes her a perfect place to slot something paranormal into history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T18:25:26-07:00","id":575856,"title":"","content":"The Predator Kings could take advantage of the weaknesses of both sides, attacking supply lines and destroying things without regard to alliance, as well as making some territories unbearable to fight on as they get amped up into hunters frenzy. The Ivory Claws are likely to exist wherever there's one family that think they're special, you don't really need nobility or aristocracy there, and since they started offering land to soldiers as payment wolves who thought more in the long term or who wanted to expand their family's holdings would probably try for that. While some believe the revolution was more about religious elements, when it came down to it, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1775%E2%80%9382_North_American_smallpox_epidemic\" target=\"_blank\">Smallpox ran rampant</a>, brought over by the English to the Americas where many people hadn't been exposed to it and in fact in 1775, there was an outbreak of it in Boston. Rumors spouted that the British were purposely spreading it, so the disease aspect of the Fire Touched, providing it still remains one of their domains, comes into play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-01-2015, 11:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T18:56:33-07:00","id":583003,"title":"","content":"If you're looking for spirit court conflicts I would remind you that the Europeans would have brought spirits of the old world with them and the spirits of the new would have welcomed them with open jaws.<br /> Predator Kings would be perfect to be the Hessian mercenaries, think of the description of the headless horseman while he still lived; &quot;A warrior who delighted in death and bloodshed&quot;. Such a group would make for wonderful roaming terrors that show up at the worst possible times.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T19:46:27-07:00","id":583085,"title":"","content":"Also recall that now, packs consist of more than the Uratha. The Pure could absolutely try to target any known wolf-blooded or human pack members for conversion or elimination, the latter of which could easily be covered up via the vicissitudes of war.<br /> <br /> Speaking of war and the non-werewolf pack members (although this isn't limited to them necessarily) - maybe not everyone in the pack is clearly on one side or the other. It's possible that a story concentrating on the entire pack (hunting nucleus and the rest) and their political leanings would be interesting to go through. Depends on your players, obviously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T04:25:48-07:00","id":583352,"title":"","content":"I would only point out that in <b>Hunter: The Vigil</b> we have a Candle Compact of hunters created in those years and connected to Founding Fathers - interesting would be their interplay with Pure and Iron Masters of the era. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}